Support runtime values and reference inspection in TokenScript

I'd like to use TokenScript's runtime values and inspect token references in our design-token tooling. Completing this support in `@tokens-studio/tokenscript-interpreter` would let us work with collections and colors, supply application values to expressions, and turn computed results back into JavaScript data.

For example, reference inspection and interpretation should work together like this:

```ts
import { collectReferenceNodes, Interpreter, parseExpression } from "@tokens-studio/tokenscript-interpreter/interpreter";
const source = "{spacing.base} * 3";
const parsed = parseExpression(source);
const references = collectReferenceNodes(parsed.ast!);
const runtime = new Interpreter(parsed.ast!, { references: { "spacing.base": 6 } });
const value = runtime.interpret();
```

This should let callers discover the references used by an expression and interpret it with supplied token values. The expected behaviour is described in the existing doc comments; the "Interpretation" and "Permutation with Schemas" sections in `README.md` show how this fits into token processing.

Reference collection and runtime-value operations currently throw `new Error("not implemented")`. Within `src/interpreter/`, the affected files are `symbols.ts`, `ast.ts`, `interpreter.ts`, `lexer.ts`, `config/managers/color/manager.ts`, `utils/string.ts`, and `utils/type.ts`; related helper stubs are in `tests/interpreter/test-helpers.ts`. Complete
